1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,825
Never ship to production on a single click.

2
00:00:03,375 --> 00:00:06,127
A bad release can cost a company a whole day.

3
00:00:06,127 --> 00:00:07,167
Customers see it,

4
00:00:07,167 --> 00:00:08,145
the phones ring,

5
00:00:08,145 --> 00:00:09,307
and everybody asks,

6
00:00:09,307 --> 00:00:10,714
who pressed the button?

7
00:00:11,264 --> 00:00:12,970
A good pipeline has a gate.

8
00:00:12,970 --> 00:00:13,539
It stops,

9
00:00:13,539 --> 00:00:15,687
and waits for a person to say yes.

10
00:00:15,687 --> 00:00:18,909
It moves a build forward one environment at a time.

11
00:00:18,909 --> 00:00:20,552
It can go back in seconds.

12
00:00:20,552 --> 00:00:22,827
And it tells the team what happened.

13
00:00:23,377 --> 00:00:26,917
Today you build all four in real Jenkins: an approval,

14
00:00:26,917 --> 00:00:27,703
a promotion,

15
00:00:27,703 --> 00:00:28,424
a rollback,

16
00:00:28,424 --> 00:00:29,670
and a notification.

17
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:32,649
Here is what to expect.

18
00:00:33,199 --> 00:00:37,679
One: the four ideas. Approval, promotion, rollback, notification.

19
00:00:38,229 --> 00:00:40,619
Two: how they fit together, in one picture.

20
00:00:41,169 --> 00:00:42,460
Three: a live demo,

21
00:00:42,460 --> 00:00:44,364
in the real Jenkins screens.

22
00:00:44,364 --> 00:00:46,403
We pause a build for approval,

23
00:00:46,403 --> 00:00:47,695
then say no to one.

24
00:00:47,695 --> 00:00:50,958
Then we promote a real CloudCart build from dev,

25
00:00:50,958 --> 00:00:51,706
to staging,

26
00:00:51,706 --> 00:00:52,658
to production.

27
00:00:52,658 --> 00:00:54,629
Then we roll production back.

28
00:00:54,629 --> 00:00:57,553
And we watch the team notifications arrive.

29
00:00:58,103 --> 00:01:00,919
Four: the common mistakes, and where to find the lab.

30
00:01:01,469 --> 00:01:04,285
This is objective eight of the Jenkins domain.

31
00:01:05,835 --> 00:01:06,859
Four ideas.

32
00:01:07,409 --> 00:01:08,895
An approval is a gate.

33
00:01:08,895 --> 00:01:11,395
The pipeline pauses at an input step,

34
00:01:11,395 --> 00:01:13,692
and waits for a person to approve,

35
00:01:13,692 --> 00:01:14,300
or abort.

36
00:01:14,850 --> 00:01:18,836
A promotion moves the same build to the next environment: dev,

37
00:01:18,836 --> 00:01:19,672
then staging,

38
00:01:19,672 --> 00:01:20,700
then production.

39
00:01:20,700 --> 00:01:22,822
You promote the build you tested.

40
00:01:22,822 --> 00:01:24,172
You never rebuild it.

41
00:01:24,722 --> 00:01:30,056
A rollback is a way back. A job that puts the previous good version live again, fast.

42
00:01:30,606 --> 00:01:32,486
A notification tells people.

43
00:01:32,486 --> 00:01:33,157
A message,

44
00:01:33,157 --> 00:01:34,500
to chat or to email,

45
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:36,111
when a release succeeds,

46
00:01:36,111 --> 00:01:36,514
fails,

47
00:01:36,514 --> 00:01:37,454
or is stopped.

48
00:01:38,004 --> 00:01:41,588
Gate, promote, roll back, tell. That is a release you can trust.

49
00:01:43,138 --> 00:01:45,378
Here is how they fit together in our demo.

50
00:01:45,928 --> 00:01:47,160
The build runs once,

51
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:48,946
and the war file is archived.

52
00:01:48,946 --> 00:01:50,424
It goes straight to dev,

53
00:01:50,424 --> 00:01:51,224
with no gate,

54
00:01:51,224 --> 00:01:52,456
because dev is safe.

55
00:01:53,006 --> 00:01:53,920
Before staging,

56
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:54,896
there is a gate.

57
00:01:54,896 --> 00:01:55,993
A person approves.

58
00:01:55,993 --> 00:01:57,090
Before production,

59
00:01:57,090 --> 00:01:58,492
there is a second gate,

60
00:01:58,492 --> 00:02:00,686
and only an admin may press release.

61
00:02:01,236 --> 00:02:03,334
Each environment gets the same file.

62
00:02:03,334 --> 00:02:05,724
Production points at the current release,

63
00:02:05,724 --> 00:02:07,764
with a link called current.war.

64
00:02:08,314 --> 00:02:11,846
Rollback is just moving that link back to an older release.

65
00:02:11,846 --> 00:02:12,983
Nothing is rebuilt,

66
00:02:12,983 --> 00:02:14,181
so it takes seconds.

67
00:02:14,731 --> 00:02:19,083
And at the end, success, failure, or stopped, a message goes out to the team.

68
00:02:20,633 --> 00:02:21,663
A real Jenkins,

69
00:02:21,663 --> 00:02:22,967
signed in as admin.

70
00:02:22,967 --> 00:02:24,545
The dashboard is empty.

71
00:02:24,545 --> 00:02:26,742
Everything you see in this demo,

72
00:02:26,742 --> 00:02:27,634
I create now,

73
00:02:27,634 --> 00:02:28,526
from scratch.

74
00:02:32,276 --> 00:02:32,721
First,

75
00:02:32,721 --> 00:02:34,054
the simplest gate.

76
00:02:34,054 --> 00:02:34,721
New Item.

77
00:02:34,721 --> 00:02:35,462
I name it,

78
00:02:35,462 --> 00:02:36,573
hello approval.

79
00:02:36,573 --> 00:02:38,129
The type is Pipeline,

80
00:02:38,129 --> 00:02:40,129
a script that Jenkins runs,

81
00:02:40,129 --> 00:02:41,092
step by step.

82
00:02:41,092 --> 00:02:41,684
Then OK.

83
00:02:43,534 --> 00:02:45,446
The script has three stages.

84
00:02:45,446 --> 00:02:45,855
Build,

85
00:02:45,855 --> 00:02:46,402
Approve,

86
00:02:46,402 --> 00:02:47,152
and Deploy.

87
00:02:47,152 --> 00:02:49,269
The Approve stage has one step,

88
00:02:49,269 --> 00:02:49,678
input.

89
00:02:49,678 --> 00:02:54,457
It is a built in step that pauses the pipeline until a person answers.

90
00:02:54,457 --> 00:02:56,368
Its message is the question,

91
00:02:56,368 --> 00:02:57,597
deploy to staging.

92
00:02:57,597 --> 00:02:59,714
And its ok button says Approve.

93
00:02:59,714 --> 00:03:02,171
Each stage is a box in the pipeline,

94
00:03:02,171 --> 00:03:03,673
and they run in order.

95
00:03:05,923 --> 00:03:06,267
Save,

96
00:03:06,267 --> 00:03:07,297
then Build Now.

97
00:03:07,297 --> 00:03:09,427
The build runs the first stage,

98
00:03:09,427 --> 00:03:10,938
then reaches the gate.

99
00:03:10,938 --> 00:03:12,106
Open the console.

100
00:03:12,106 --> 00:03:13,961
Here the build has stopped.

101
00:03:13,961 --> 00:03:16,022
The last line is the question,

102
00:03:16,022 --> 00:03:17,259
deploy to staging,

103
00:03:17,259 --> 00:03:19,045
with two choices: Approve,

104
00:03:19,045 --> 00:03:19,663
or Abort.

105
00:03:19,663 --> 00:03:22,136
Nothing runs until a person answers.

106
00:03:22,686 --> 00:03:23,707
I click Approve.

107
00:03:23,707 --> 00:03:25,174
The pipeline continues.

108
00:03:25,174 --> 00:03:26,577
The Deploy stage runs,

109
00:03:26,577 --> 00:03:28,044
and the build finishes,

110
00:03:28,044 --> 00:03:28,873
with success.

111
00:03:29,423 --> 00:03:34,287
Now the other answer. Build Now again. Open the console, and wait for the question.

112
00:03:36,037 --> 00:03:37,726
This time I click Abort.

113
00:03:37,726 --> 00:03:38,852
The build stops.

114
00:03:38,852 --> 00:03:40,822
The Deploy stage never runs.

115
00:03:40,822 --> 00:03:42,371
In the list of builds,

116
00:03:42,371 --> 00:03:43,919
the result is aborted,

117
00:03:43,919 --> 00:03:44,271
grey,

118
00:03:44,271 --> 00:03:44,834
not red.

119
00:03:44,834 --> 00:03:46,030
A person said no.

120
00:03:46,030 --> 00:03:47,578
That is not a failure.

121
00:03:57,228 --> 00:03:58,479
Now a real release.

122
00:03:58,479 --> 00:03:59,466
A new Pipeline,

123
00:03:59,466 --> 00:04:01,112
named CloudCart release.

124
00:04:01,112 --> 00:04:02,362
Here is the script,

125
00:04:02,362 --> 00:04:03,350
in three parts.

126
00:04:03,350 --> 00:04:05,917
Stage one builds CloudCart with Maven,

127
00:04:05,917 --> 00:04:07,628
and archives the war file.

128
00:04:07,628 --> 00:04:10,130
Stage two copies it to the dev folder.

129
00:04:10,130 --> 00:04:11,314
Then comes a gate,

130
00:04:11,314 --> 00:04:12,565
promote to staging,

131
00:04:12,565 --> 00:04:14,145
and the copy to staging.

132
00:04:14,145 --> 00:04:15,395
Then a second gate,

133
00:04:15,395 --> 00:04:16,843
release to production.

134
00:04:16,843 --> 00:04:20,990
This one has submitter admin: only the user admin may press it.

135
00:04:20,990 --> 00:04:21,319
Last,

136
00:04:21,319 --> 00:04:23,689
the production stage copies the war,

137
00:04:23,689 --> 00:04:26,388
and moves the link current.war to it.

138
00:04:26,388 --> 00:04:27,572
And at the bottom,

139
00:04:27,572 --> 00:04:28,691
the post section.

140
00:04:28,691 --> 00:04:30,403
When the release succeeds,

141
00:04:30,403 --> 00:04:31,127
is stopped,

142
00:04:31,127 --> 00:04:31,719
or fails,

143
00:04:31,719 --> 00:04:34,089
Jenkins sends a message to the team.

144
00:04:34,089 --> 00:04:35,537
We will see it arrive.

145
00:04:36,087 --> 00:04:36,440
Save,

146
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:37,427
and Build Now.

147
00:04:37,427 --> 00:04:38,626
Open the console.

148
00:04:38,626 --> 00:04:40,672
Maven is building CloudCart.

149
00:04:40,672 --> 00:04:42,999
This takes about fifteen seconds.

150
00:04:42,999 --> 00:04:44,763
Then the war is archived,

151
00:04:44,763 --> 00:04:46,033
and copied to dev.

152
00:04:46,033 --> 00:04:47,161
Dev has no gate,

153
00:04:47,161 --> 00:04:48,290
so it just goes.

154
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:52,325
Now the first gate.

155
00:04:52,325 --> 00:04:53,611
Promote to staging.

156
00:04:53,611 --> 00:04:54,694
I click Approve.

157
00:04:54,694 --> 00:04:57,333
The same war file is copied to staging.

158
00:04:57,883 --> 00:04:58,927
The second gate.

159
00:04:58,927 --> 00:05:00,362
Release to production.

160
00:05:00,362 --> 00:05:01,406
I click Release.

161
00:05:01,406 --> 00:05:02,581
The war is copied,

162
00:05:02,581 --> 00:05:03,821
and the link moves.

163
00:05:03,821 --> 00:05:05,126
Look at the listing.

164
00:05:05,126 --> 00:05:08,649
current.war points to cloudcart-1.war.

165
00:05:08,649 --> 00:05:09,889
That is production,

166
00:05:09,889 --> 00:05:10,150
now.

167
00:05:10,700 --> 00:05:16,140
Success. And look at the last lines. Jenkins posted the message to the team, using curl.

168
00:05:28,690 --> 00:05:29,485
Release two.

169
00:05:29,485 --> 00:05:30,545
Build Now again,

170
00:05:30,545 --> 00:05:32,070
and approve both gates,

171
00:05:32,070 --> 00:05:33,263
exactly as before.

172
00:05:33,263 --> 00:05:34,190
First Approve,

173
00:05:34,190 --> 00:05:35,052
then Release.

174
00:05:35,052 --> 00:05:37,570
The build takes about fifteen seconds,

175
00:05:37,570 --> 00:05:39,426
so I wait for each question.

176
00:05:39,426 --> 00:05:41,746
The link now points to release two.

177
00:05:46,296 --> 00:05:48,528
Now suppose release two has a bug,

178
00:05:48,528 --> 00:05:50,301
and customers are shouting.

179
00:05:50,301 --> 00:05:51,877
We need production back,

180
00:05:51,877 --> 00:05:52,140
now.

181
00:05:52,140 --> 00:05:53,125
A new Pipeline,

182
00:05:53,125 --> 00:05:54,833
named CloudCart rollback.

183
00:05:54,833 --> 00:05:56,015
It is a small job,

184
00:05:56,015 --> 00:05:58,050
and it does one thing: go back.

185
00:06:02,700 --> 00:06:04,049
It has one parameter,

186
00:06:04,049 --> 00:06:04,563
version,

187
00:06:04,563 --> 00:06:06,425
with the choices two and one.

188
00:06:06,425 --> 00:06:10,793
The only stage moves the link current.war to the chosen release,

189
00:06:10,793 --> 00:06:12,527
and prints where it points.

190
00:06:12,527 --> 00:06:13,747
Nothing is rebuilt.

191
00:06:13,747 --> 00:06:14,068
Save,

192
00:06:14,068 --> 00:06:14,967
and Build Now.

193
00:06:14,967 --> 00:06:17,408
The first run registers the parameter.

194
00:06:17,408 --> 00:06:19,206
Release two is already live,

195
00:06:19,206 --> 00:06:21,004
so this run changes nothing.

196
00:06:22,654 --> 00:06:25,517
Now the button says Build with Parameters.

197
00:06:25,517 --> 00:06:26,949
I choose version one,

198
00:06:26,949 --> 00:06:27,630
and Build.

199
00:06:27,630 --> 00:06:28,789
Open the console.

200
00:06:28,789 --> 00:06:33,560
readlink says: current.war points to cloudcart-1.war.

201
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:35,878
Production is back on release one,

202
00:06:35,878 --> 00:06:36,628
in seconds.

203
00:06:37,178 --> 00:06:37,509
Last,

204
00:06:37,509 --> 00:06:38,105
the team.

205
00:06:38,105 --> 00:06:39,562
This is the lab inbox,

206
00:06:39,562 --> 00:06:41,151
running on this machine,

207
00:06:41,151 --> 00:06:43,403
on port eighty eighty ninety nine.

208
00:06:43,403 --> 00:06:45,059
Each release posted here.

209
00:06:45,059 --> 00:06:46,383
Release one is live.

210
00:06:46,383 --> 00:06:47,708
Release two is live.

211
00:06:47,708 --> 00:06:47,973
And,

212
00:06:47,973 --> 00:06:50,490
production rolled back to release one.

213
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:52,140
In your company,

214
00:06:52,140 --> 00:06:54,410
the same post step goes to Slack,

215
00:06:54,410 --> 00:06:54,823
Teams,

216
00:06:54,823 --> 00:06:55,442
or email.

217
00:06:55,442 --> 00:06:59,018
The idea is the same: a build always tells the team.

218
00:06:59,568 --> 00:07:01,572
That is a release you can trust.

219
00:07:01,572 --> 00:07:03,138
A gate before every risk.

220
00:07:03,138 --> 00:07:05,017
The same build moving forward.

221
00:07:05,017 --> 00:07:05,705
A way back.

222
00:07:05,705 --> 00:07:07,334
And a message to the team.

223
00:07:08,884 --> 00:07:10,036
Five mistakes.

224
00:07:10,586 --> 00:07:15,343
One: no gate before production. Add an input step, and limit who may approve it.

225
00:07:15,893 --> 00:07:20,523
Two: rebuilding for each environment. Build once, and promote the same file.

226
00:07:21,073 --> 00:07:23,503
Three: an input step with no timeout.

227
00:07:23,503 --> 00:07:26,328
A forgotten gate holds an executor forever.

228
00:07:26,328 --> 00:07:27,707
Wrap it in a timeout.

229
00:07:28,257 --> 00:07:32,353
Four: a rollback nobody has tried. Practise it, before the bad day.

230
00:07:32,903 --> 00:07:38,642
Five: silent pipelines. Always send a message, for success, for failure, and for stopped.

231
00:07:40,192 --> 00:07:42,987
Where to find the lab. Pause here, and write it down.

232
00:07:43,537 --> 00:07:45,001
One: the repository,

233
00:07:45,001 --> 00:07:49,321
GitHub dot com slash it dash waves slash dev ops dash A I,

234
00:07:49,321 --> 00:07:51,665
in the folder academy slash lab.

235
00:07:52,215 --> 00:07:58,231
Two: the files, lab161 dot S H, and shortcuts one sixty-one dot S H.

236
00:07:58,781 --> 00:08:04,242
Three: install it, with sudo install, into slash user slash local slash S bin.

237
00:08:04,792 --> 00:08:10,360
Four: load the short names, with source shortcuts one sixty-one dot S H. Then lab up.

238
00:08:10,910 --> 00:08:13,961
Five: lab files writes the three pipeline scripts,

239
00:08:13,961 --> 00:08:16,585
and lab hook starts the notification inbox.

240
00:08:17,135 --> 00:08:20,765
Six: you need the Jenkins from lesson one fifty-five,

241
00:08:20,765 --> 00:08:21,450
and Maven.

242
00:08:21,450 --> 00:08:24,943
Lab down stops the inbox and removes the lab files.

243
00:08:25,493 --> 00:08:27,135
The link is in the description.

244
00:08:29,185 --> 00:08:30,956
Your turn, on your own machine.

245
00:08:31,506 --> 00:08:33,852
One: lab up, lab hook, and lab files.

246
00:08:34,402 --> 00:08:38,925
Two: create hello approval, and answer it twice: once Approve, once Abort.

247
00:08:39,475 --> 00:08:44,083
Three: create CloudCart release, and promote a build all the way to production.

248
00:08:44,633 --> 00:08:48,153
Four: create CloudCart rollback, and roll production back.

249
00:08:48,703 --> 00:08:52,884
Five: open the inbox, and read your three messages. Then lab down.

250
00:08:53,434 --> 00:08:55,269
Pause the video, and begin now.

251
00:09:10,819 --> 00:09:11,694
Quick check.

252
00:09:12,244 --> 00:09:13,716
What does an input step do?

253
00:09:14,266 --> 00:09:16,954
Why promote the same build, instead of rebuilding?

254
00:09:17,504 --> 00:09:19,466
How does a rollback work in our demo?

255
00:09:20,016 --> 00:09:21,979
Why should an input step have a timeout?

256
00:09:22,529 --> 00:09:25,004
Objective covered: M C seventeen,

257
00:09:25,004 --> 00:09:26,204
objective eight.

258
00:09:26,204 --> 00:09:26,879
Approval,

259
00:09:26,879 --> 00:09:27,629
promotion,

260
00:09:27,629 --> 00:09:29,654
rollback and notifications.

261
00:09:30,204 --> 00:09:32,274
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

262
00:09:42,824 --> 00:09:45,896
Next: backup, upgrade and troubleshooting Jenkins.

263
00:09:46,446 --> 00:09:49,774
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
